{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794761415,"nonce":"Kr4k442ETkdHFjuLOZgAkssaj+s=","title":"Link Ash wasm libraries with Ash's linker, not rust-lld side modules","message":"Decided by the user on 2026-11-15: for hl --wasm, hxn should build the library as a static archive and have Ash link it into main.wasm with --native-lib, as it does for Android and iOS, dropping the rust-lld side-module link. rust-lld is the only reason an Ash wasm build needs llvm-tools on macOS (it loads libLLVM.dylib from rustlib/\u003chost\u003e/lib), and Ash's own build of the program has no LLVM in it.\n\nBlocked on Ash. Its wasm linker takes wasm objects only: --native-lib libgreeter_hl.a fails with \"magic header not detected\". Passing the archive's members (llvm-ar x) as separate objects gets to \"errno is defined in both hxn_hl-...rcgu.o and ash_runtime.o\" (hxn-hl's own errno, which a static link would drop), then \"rust_eh_personality is defined in both std-...cgu.10.rcgu.o and ash_runtime.o\": forcing every member in brings the archive's build-std copy of std alongside the runtime's. What hxn needs is archive semantics in ash_wasm_link: read an ar archive with GNU long names, pull members only for undefined symbols, the runtime object's definitions winning, ash_host_* left as host imports. Asked of Ash's session (ash-29), which is putting it to its user.\n\nWhen Ash has it: build the wasm staticlib without the side module's errno, pass the archive to ash --build, ship lib\u003cname\u003e.a under native/\u003cwasm triple\u003e/ as for mobile, keep page/ beside the program, and drop the llvm-tools requirement from docs/cli.md, hxn doctor and libraries' CI.","files":null}]}